# vscode

> HTML shelf named vscode. Sister of custom-vscode and vscode-oss-dev.

## Purpose
Give a plain-language door to fitzyracing1/vscode.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Keep the original repo as the place for files.
2. Use this clone to explain the idea.
3. Send the reader to the sister shelves if needed.

## Key ideas
- vscode (the named shelf)
- HTML source

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/vscode
open_source()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. open_source() → “go to fitzyracing1/vscode”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a reader wants a sister shelf → custom-vscode or vscode-oss-dev

## What a person would notice
A named wrap on a vscode door.

